{"availability":"available","full":"baconjs/bacon.js","name":"bacon.js","description":"Functional reactive programming library for TypeScript and JavaScript","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":6453,"forks":328,"created":"2012-03-02T19:21:42Z","updated":"2025-04-18T11:27:53Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://baconjs.github.io","topics":[],"demo":"https://baconjs.github.io/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:36.739Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:36.739Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:36.739Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T13:03:36.739Z","stars":6453,"forks":328}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A functional reactive programming lib for TypeScript JavaScript, written in TypeScript.","Turns your event spaghetti into clean and declarative feng shui bacon, by switching from imperative to functional. It's like replacing nested for-loops with functional programming concepts like map and filter. Stop working on individual events and work with event streams instead. Combine your data with merge and combine. Then switch to the heavier weapons and wield flatMap and combineTemplate like a boss.","Bacon.js exists largely because I got frustrated with RxJs, which is a good library, but at that time didn't have very good documentation and wasn't open-source. Things have improved a lot in the Rx world since that. Yet, there are still compelling reasons to use Bacon.js instead. Like, for instance,"],"features":["Generated javascript","Wiki with more docs, related projects and more","Gitter chat for developers of Bacon.","more consistent stream/property behavior"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/baconjs/bacon.js/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"5591a3bb3bb8bbe9c621442f658c7c4d05595dc8ca6a75ff16c21fa6c6b158fa","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:36.862Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:36.862Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A